{
  "_comment": [
    "Cimmeria MCP server configuration template.",
    "",
    "Copy this file to .mcp.json (which is gitignored) and replace the",
    "<CIMMERIA_ROOT> placeholders with the absolute path to your repo checkout.",
    "On Windows that looks like: C:\\Users\\you\\source\\projects\\Cimmeria",
    "",
    "If you ran `pwsh setup.ps1 -WithReToolchain`, this file was generated for",
    "you automatically. See:",
    "  docs/guides/re-toolchain-setup.md     -- end-to-end setup",
    "  docs/guides/reverse-engineering-with-claude.md  -- the workflow doc",
    "  docs/guides/live-research-lab.md      -- the lab runbook",
    "",
    "Four servers are wired (mcpServers below):",
    "  ghidra       : Static analysis of SGW.exe via the bethington/ghidra-mcp",
    "                 bridge. Requires Ghidra GUI running with the GhidraMCP",
    "                 plugin server started.",
    "  x64dbg       : Dynamic analysis via dariushoule/x64dbg-automate. Requires",
    "                 x96dbg.exe launched with the x64dbg-automate plugin loaded.",
    "  cimmeria-lab : the Live Research Lab supervisor, as ONE shared daemon",
    "                 for every session (cimmeria-lab --http, a per-user",
    "                 scheduled task). Set it up with: pwsh tools/lab/cli/local-setup.ps1, then",
    "                 pwsh tools/lab/install.ps1, then",
    "                 pwsh tools/lab/daemon.ps1 install. Loopback only; the",
    "                 bearer token comes from labd-headers.ps1, which reads the",
    "                 CIMMERIA_LAB_DAEMON_TOKEN user env var (daemon.ps1",
    "                 install generates it). Keep the timeout (ms): it lifts",
    "                 Claude Code's 60 s per-request timer for HTTP servers,",
    "                 which cut lab_uat_run rows off. One daemon serves every",
    "                 lab account: tools take an optional instance (default,",
    "                 p2, ... or lab, lab2, ...).",
    "  lab-server   : In-server lab endpoint (http, token-gated). Live entity /",
    "                 witness / packet-tap / dot-console reads from a running",
    "                 cimmeria-server. Only present when the server was started",
    "                 with CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_BIND + CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_TOKEN set",
    "                 (fail-closed). Locally that is 127.0.0.1:8451 (8444 is",
    "                 the dev supervisor's port); on the colo it is reachable",
    "                 over WireGuard only -- see docs/operations/colo-deploy.md.",
    "                 URL and token come from the CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_URL /",
    "                 CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_TOKEN user env vars (Claude Code expands",
    "                 ${VAR} here), so the token never lands in this file.",
    "",
    "_alternatives (ignored by Claude Code; copy an entry into mcpServers to",
    "use it):",
    "  cimmeria-lab-stdio : the older one-supervisor-per-session setup. Rename",
    "                 it to cimmeria-lab in place of the daemon entry. Paths",
    "                 are where tools/lab/install.ps1 installs the binaries;",
    "                 <SGW_INSTALL_DIR> is the folder holding Binaries\\SGW.exe.",
    "  cimmeria-lab-p2 : a second stdio supervisor for a second lab client.",
    "                 The daemon hosts several clients itself",
    "                 (CIMMERIA_LAB_INSTANCES in labd.env), so it needs none.",
    "",
    "The GHIDRA_MCP_URL port can drift on Windows when iphlpsvc holds 8089-8099.",
    "The plugin falls back to the first free port in 8089..8104 — confirm the",
    "actual bound port from Ghidra's console output, not the status dialog",
    "(upstream display bug shows the configured port, not the bound one)."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "ghidra": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "<CIMMERIA_ROOT>\\.venvs\\ghidra-mcp\\Scripts\\python.exe",
      "args": [
        "<CIMMERIA_ROOT>\\external\\ghidra-mcp\\bridge_mcp_ghidra.py"
      ],
      "env": {
        "GHIDRA_MCP_URL": "http://127.0.0.1:8100/"
      }
    },
    "x64dbg": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "<CIMMERIA_ROOT>\\.venvs\\x64dbg-mcp\\Scripts\\x64dbg-automate-mcp.exe",
      "env": {
        "X64DBG_PATH": "<CIMMERIA_ROOT>\\dbg\\release\\x96dbg.exe"
      }
    },
    "cimmeria-lab": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8779/mcp",
      "headersHelper": "pwsh -NoProfile -File \"<CIMMERIA_ROOT>\\tools\\lab\\labd-headers.ps1\"",
      "timeout": 1800000
    },
    "lab-server": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "${CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:8451/mcp}",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer ${CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_TOKEN:-}"
      }
    }
  },
  "_alternatives": {
    "cimmeria-lab-stdio": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "<LAB_BIN>\\cimmeria-lab.exe",
      "env": {
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_INSTALL_DIR": "<SGW_INSTALL_DIR>",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_START32": "<LAB_BIN>\\sgw-start32.exe",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_BRIDGE": "127.0.0.1:8770",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_PATCHES_DLL": "<LAB_BIN>\\cimmeria_client_patches.dll",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_URL": "${CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:8451/mcp}",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_TOKEN": "${CIMMERIA_LAB_MCP_TOKEN:-}"
      }
    },
    "cimmeria-lab-p2": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "<LAB_BIN>\\cimmeria-lab.exe",
      "env": {
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_INSTANCE": "p2",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_BRIDGE_PORT": "8771",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_INSTALL_DIR": "<SGW_INSTALL_DIR>",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_START32": "<LAB_BIN>\\sgw-start32.exe",
        "CIMMERIA_LAB_PATCHES_DLL": "<LAB_BIN>\\cimmeria_client_patches.dll"
      }
    }
  }
}
